Phishing is the act of sending fraudulent emails or messages that appear to be from a legitimate source in order to obtain personal information from people. It can also include fake websites that are designed to look like a legitimate website, such as a bank or online retailer, in order to trick people into providing their personal information. People should be cautious of any email or website that asks for personal information and should verify the identity of the sender or website before providing any sensitive information. They should also be aware of any spelling mistakes or poor grammar, as well as suspicious links in emails, which could indicate a phishing attempt. It is also important to use strong passwords and two-factor authentication whenever possible to protect personal data.assistant

